    {
      "id": "RGSE",
      "code_hash": "18e0847a5e475ef9d714991979873640",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">The same rows on every engine, and the NULL key matches nothing. A node\nkeeps its state between refreshes, so the next refresh may use another\nengine than the last one. Contracts checked on the data can name an\nengine too:</span>\n<div class=\"language-python codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">node</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">refresh</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">engine</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"polars\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>   <span class=\"c1\"># or \"datafusion\", \"spark\", a SparkSession</span>\n\n<span class=\"nd\">@sv</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">transform</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ensures</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"o\">...</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"n\">on_unproved</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"runtime\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">engine</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"duckdb\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">step</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">orders</span><span class=\"p\">):</span> <span class=\"o\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"sql-for-duckdb-snowflake-and-spark\">SQL for DuckDB, Snowflake and Spark</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Often the data already lives in a warehouse, and the plan has to go to\nit rather than the other way round. The SQL generator,\n<code>sverify.engines.to_sql</code>, writes a checked plan, or one of Lean's update plans, as SQL whose\nresult is <code>Rel.eval</code> of the plan. Nothing is left to engine defaults:\ncolumns are positional (<code>c0</code>, <code>c1</code>, \u2026), filters keep only TRUE rows (<code>IS\nTRUE</code>), integers are checked against 64 bits, every <code>ORDER BY</code> says\nwhere NULLs go. Each engine's differences go through a <code>Dialect</code>:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
